;; Two three-tile gaps (5-7, 14-16), each with the deep drop two rows under
;; its lower bank and the eastward gust over it; each eastward leg lands a
;; tile higher, so the gust is what carries it and the way back west drops
;; easily in calm. A six-tile rest between them gives a real run-up. J's
;; steady lift (21-23) lands on the east bank, out of the wind.
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (12 -1)
  title: "The Open Crossing"
  intent: "eastward gusts cross two exposed breaks, with a sheltered rest between their drifts"
  bed: (wind 0.9 water 0 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "######             ######"
   "###                  ####"
   "#                       #"
   "#                    ^^^#"
   "                  | |^^^#"
   "         | |     ####^^^#"
   " |      ######   ####^^^#"
   "#####   ######   ####^^^#"
   "#####   ######xxx####^^^#"
   "#####xxx#############^^^#")
  things: ((air-field at: (5 1) size: (3 8) kind: east-gust)
           (air-field at: (14 1) size: (3 7) kind: east-gust))
  decor: auto)
